# Goals App — Multi-Container Docker Project

A simple **Goal Tracking** application built to practice combining multiple Docker building blocks — Images, Containers, Volumes, and Networking — into one realistic, multi-service application.

This project is composed of **3 independent services**, each running in its own container:

| Service   | Tech Stack           | Role                                      |
|-----------|-----------------------|--------------------------------------------|
| Database  | MongoDB (official image) | Stores the goals data                    |
| Backend   | Node.js + Express (REST API) | Handles add / fetch / delete goal logic |
| Frontend  | React (SPA)           | UI that talks to the Backend API          |

The Frontend never talks to the Database directly — it only communicates with the Backend, and the Backend is the only service that talks to MongoDB.

```
React (Frontend) → Node/Express (Backend) → MongoDB (Database)
```

---

## Architecture

- **MongoDB** runs in its own container, based on the official `mongo` image.
- **Backend** is a custom Node.js/Express REST API (no HTML/GUI — only JSON), Dockerized with a custom `Dockerfile`.
- **Frontend** is a React Single Page Application, Dockerized with its own `Dockerfile`. Note: React code executes in the **browser**, not inside the container — only the development server runs inside the container.

All three containers are connected through a custom Docker network (`goals-net`) so they can reach each other by container name instead of relying on the host machine.

---

## Prerequisites

- [Docker](https://www.docker.com/) installed and running
- No need to install MongoDB, Node, or React dependencies locally — everything runs inside containers

---

